  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Latha Devi vs The Designated Officer on 9 February, 2024 Author: S.M.Subramaniam Bench: S.M.Subramaniam W.P.No In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 09.02.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice S.M.Subramaniam W.P. No.13017 of 2020 and W.M.P.No.16129 of 2020 Latha Devi ... Petit Vs. 1.The Designated Officer, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration Department Race Course Road, Coimbatore-641 018, Coimbatore District. 2.The Food Safety Officer, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug, Administration Department, Coimbatore Urban, Coimbatore District. 3.B.Ashok ... Respo Prayer: Writ Petition is filed under Article 226 of the Constitutio to issue a Writ of Mandamus, directing the respondents 1 and 2 to d the petitioner's property at No.56, Ponnusamy Lay out, Krishna Naga Page 1 of 5 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W. Latha Devi vs The Designated Officer on 9 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/181193620/ 1 Coimbatore -1 sealed by the respondent-2 in and by a form of seizur 16.08.2018 after clearing all the banned products stocked by the Th respondent in a manner known to law. For Petitioner : Mr.P.Manojkumar For R1 & R2 : Mr.K.Tippu Sulthan Government Advocate For R3 : Not ready in notice Order Mr.K.Tippu Sulthan, learned Government Advocate appearing on behalf of the 1st and 2nd respondents would submit that the building belongs to the writ petitioner was inspected and the Food Safety Offic",
    "facts": "ers have found that the 3rd respondent was a tenant and in possession of the subject building. A case was registered against the 3rd respondent, since the 3rd respondent has stocked up banned Tobacco and Pan Masala. The tobacco products seized by the Tamil Nadu Food Safety officers may be shifted to any other Government godown or it may be destroyed by following the procedures as contemplated by preserving samples as per the provisions of the Act and Rules.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
